{"id": 61, "ts": 1779894183.0572062, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 4, "agent": "agent_1", "message": "I remain convinced that Candidate\u202fC is the strongest overall fit. As the panel has highlighted, C is\u202f100\u202f% reliable, makes correct decisions quickly, and \u201ckeeps calm in a crisis,\u201d covering the core safety criteria of operational reliability, decision quality, and stress resilience. The recent confirmation that C \u201cunderstands complicated technology\u201d adds the missing technical\u2011cognitive competence, while his ability to create a positive crew atmosphere demonstrates solid crew cooperation and professional communication. In contrast, Candidate\u202fA lacks any documented evidence of operational reliability or crew\u2011cooperation and is noted as unorganized and resistant to criticism\u2014critical gaps for long\u2011haul flights. Candidate\u202fD, although responsible and focused, shows no concrete crew\u2011cooperation evidence and is described as arrogant with weak leadership, raising teamwork concerns. Candidate\u202fB, while stress\u2011resilient and technically capable, has documented \u201cnasty remarks\u201d and a weak memory for numbers, indicating risks to cockpit cohesion and attention to detail. Given that C meets all major safety\u2011critical criteria and the remaining concerns (egocentric attitude, limited education willingness) are outweighed by his proven strengths, I continue to recommend Candidate\u202fC for the long\u2011distance pilot position."}
